<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#devanagari">Glossary</a> · Term · script</p><h1 class="enc-title">Devanagari</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Devanagari is an Indian script, written from left to right with a characteristic horizontal headline, in which each consonant carries an inherent vowel. It developed from the Brahmi script through the Nagari scripts of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in the late first millennium CE. It is used for Hindi, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marathi">Marathi</a>, Nepali, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> and many other languages and is one of the most widely used writing systems in the world.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/devanagari.jpg" alt="Devanagari" width="320" height="632" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Symphonicallyu · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Devanagari_Varnamala.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
